The dish looks like a bowl about 15 cm across. It holds braised meat, which appears to be beef, on a bed of diced roasted squash or sweet potato with herbs. The portion is moderate, roughly 200 g in total, made up of about 80 g of meat and 120 g of vegetables.

For energy, braised beef is about 2.2 kcal/g, so 80 g gives roughly 175 kcal. The diced vegetables with some oil are about 1.0 kcal/g, so 120 g gives roughly 120 kcal. That totals about 295 kcal, and I'll round it to 300.

